WEBVTT

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:39.182
You guys are from Court 2, aren't you?

00:01:40.183 --> 00:01:41.726
What about it?

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.312
Hey...

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:48.400
Why don't we play a match?

00:01:54.447 --> 00:02:00.453
"Towards Your New Brilliant Selves"

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.963
You're at it bright and early.

00:02:13.508 --> 00:02:16.720
By the way, an interesting
match is about to start.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:26.813
They came down from
the mountain, didn't they?

00:02:32.861 --> 00:02:35.739
We have a rule at this training camp.

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:36.656
What rule?

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:40.326
We must not refuse a challenge

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.828
from those wearing black jerseys.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.747
How dramatic.

00:02:43.747 --> 00:02:46.916
Probability Coach Nyudo
created this rule...

00:02:46.916 --> 00:02:48.543
...100%.

00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:51.212
They're almost like phantoms.

00:02:51.212 --> 00:02:56.134
Branded as losers,
former members of this camp

00:02:56.134 --> 00:02:58.970
return suddenly in black jerseys.

00:02:59.554 --> 00:03:03.350
Having improved their skills
drastically since they left,

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.769
they're not far off from Court 1.

00:03:06.353 --> 00:03:07.812
Some call them

00:03:07.812 --> 00:03:10.398
"the Black Jerseys who
found their way back."

00:03:10.398 --> 00:03:14.694
Isn't there something better
you could call us?

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:17.822
"The Black Jerseys who somehow
found their way back," then.

00:03:18.114 --> 00:03:19.282
Forget it.

00:03:19.282 --> 00:03:20.658
Let's just play.

00:03:21.284 --> 00:03:23.244
We came all the way back here,

00:03:23.244 --> 00:03:25.246
but we don't have anywhere to practice.

00:03:26.456 --> 00:03:28.583
We're taking Court 2.

00:03:30.293 --> 00:03:32.754
No matter how many players
you throw at us,

00:03:32.754 --> 00:03:35.507
you'll never beat Court 2.

00:03:36.257 --> 00:03:40.136
If we lose even a single game,
we'll consider it our loss.

00:03:40.136 --> 00:03:41.179
What?

00:03:41.179 --> 00:03:44.349
None of us will lose to you.

00:03:45.183 --> 00:03:47.268
What'd you say?

00:03:47.602 --> 00:03:49.896
Don't get ahead of yourselves!

00:03:57.028 --> 00:03:58.613
Wh-What's going on?

00:04:00.782 --> 00:04:02.033
Impossible.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:06.746
He returned them all himself.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.998
Good going, Tanishi.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:12.752
Very well.

00:04:13.378 --> 00:04:17.799
Let's see if the Black Jerseys
are as good as the rumors say.

00:04:32.147 --> 00:04:36.860
Nothing beats a cup of Single Estate
tea after a workout like that.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:39.362
Big news!

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:43.366
Kikumaru-<i>kun</i>, you're awfully
noisy this morning.

00:04:44.409 --> 00:04:47.704
Court 2's starting a match.

00:04:47.704 --> 00:04:49.039
Court 2?

00:04:50.415 --> 00:04:54.169
Do we have a shuffle match
against Court 2 today?

00:04:54.169 --> 00:04:56.963
No, Onigawara said we wouldn't be

00:04:56.963 --> 00:05:00.383
having any shuffle matches for a while.

00:05:00.925 --> 00:05:03.428
Then are they playing Court 1?

00:05:03.428 --> 00:05:06.931
No, they're playing Oishi,
shorty, and the others.

00:05:06.931 --> 00:05:12.103
The guys who supposedly left
the camp are playing Court 2.

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:17.275
Snake!

00:05:21.863 --> 00:05:23.865
Burning!

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:30.205
Good job.

00:05:30.205 --> 00:05:32.540
I bet that thing's stronger

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:34.542
than Gin's 108 styles of Hadokyu.

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:38.588
Did these guys really
fail out of this camp?

00:05:46.429 --> 00:05:50.767
Over already? This is no fun.

00:05:51.518 --> 00:05:52.686
Kin-<i>chan</i>.

00:05:56.064 --> 00:05:57.232
Oishi.

00:06:14.457 --> 00:06:18.336
Not enough. Not nearly enough.

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:19.671
Momo.

00:06:20.255 --> 00:06:22.507
Shishido-<i>san</i>... Shishido-<i>san</i>.

00:06:29.848 --> 00:06:32.684
Is this the best Court 2 can do?

00:06:33.977 --> 00:06:35.186
You must be going soft!

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:45.113
They've improved far
more than we expected.

00:06:50.285 --> 00:06:51.786
The rest is up to you.

00:06:52.537 --> 00:06:53.747
Gotcha.

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:58.376
We can't win a single game.

00:06:58.376 --> 00:07:01.588
They're too strong.

00:07:02.714 --> 00:07:06.509
Huh? No one's coming to the court?

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:10.180
Then I guess we've won.

00:07:26.613 --> 00:07:28.198
I knew it.

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:32.118
You're the strongest member
of Court 2, aren't you?

00:07:34.496 --> 00:07:35.955
Play me.

00:07:36.498 --> 00:07:39.918
Migihashi, go show 'em who's boss!

00:07:39.918 --> 00:07:41.586
They've made us Court 2
members look like...

00:07:41.586 --> 00:07:44.172
After all the games you lost,

00:07:44.172 --> 00:07:46.049
you have no right to call yourselves
members of this court.

00:07:51.012 --> 00:07:52.389
Let's get started.

00:08:02.607 --> 00:08:05.902
They've had to bring out their
court leader, Migihashi.

00:08:05.902 --> 00:08:08.822
Not bad, Black Jerseys.

00:08:12.075 --> 00:08:13.493
What's going on?

00:08:13.493 --> 00:08:15.370
His right side's wide open.

00:08:23.712 --> 00:08:26.548
His right's even more open.

00:08:30.885 --> 00:08:32.929
All right. You got him this time.

00:08:35.682 --> 00:08:36.433
What?

00:08:36.433 --> 00:08:38.435
He returned it.

00:08:39.352 --> 00:08:42.355
My right side is God's Domain.

00:08:42.355 --> 00:08:44.858
Nothing gets past it.

00:08:45.316 --> 00:08:46.609
God's Domain?

00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:48.778
He may call it that,

00:08:48.778 --> 00:08:51.781
but he's probably just bad
at hitting backhand.

00:08:51.781 --> 00:08:54.200
Echizen, break through the left!

00:08:58.538 --> 00:09:01.875
All right! Now cross to his left!

00:09:02.584 --> 00:09:04.669
You still have a long way to go.

00:09:07.714 --> 00:09:10.675
Koshimae, why don't you
hit to his left side?

00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:17.182
No one can get anything past
Migihashi's right side.

00:09:20.852 --> 00:09:21.770
The right side again.

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:23.188
What the hell are you doing?!

00:09:27.359 --> 00:09:31.321
It seems Echizen is being
forced to hit to the right.

00:09:31.321 --> 00:09:32.697
Forced?

00:09:32.989 --> 00:09:35.533
He's putting spin on his
opponent's ball to prevent it

00:09:35.533 --> 00:09:37.827
from going to his left side.

00:09:37.827 --> 00:09:41.623
Isn't that... Tezuka Zone?

00:09:41.623 --> 00:09:44.542
The mechanism he's
using must be similar.

00:09:48.546 --> 00:09:50.048
Right Saver.

00:09:51.925 --> 00:09:56.388
That right side defense is unforgiving.

00:10:00.266 --> 00:10:04.104
Normally you wouldn't let anyone hit
to your left, since it's a blind spot.

00:10:04.437 --> 00:10:10.026
The probability of Echizen hitting
to his left is close to 0%.

00:10:10.026 --> 00:10:11.027
Then...

00:10:11.361 --> 00:10:12.404
He has no blind spots.

00:10:14.739 --> 00:10:18.243
Hey, you can stop hitting those.

00:10:20.203 --> 00:10:22.497
I promise I'll break through your right side.

00:10:26.167 --> 00:10:28.670
In fact, I'm only gonna hit to your right.

00:10:30.296 --> 00:10:32.340
I knew you'd go for that.

00:10:39.305 --> 00:10:41.808
L-Love-Fifteen.

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:49.649
You'll break through my right?

00:10:49.649 --> 00:10:51.109
Big talk.

00:11:00.493 --> 00:11:05.331
It seems you can return
multiple balls at once.

00:11:06.624 --> 00:11:08.126
What're you talking about?

00:11:08.126 --> 00:11:11.379
Koshimae can hit eight at once.

00:11:11.379 --> 00:11:12.339
Eight?

00:11:14.007 --> 00:11:15.550
Interesting.

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:20.388
If you can hit just one ball
past my right, you win.

00:11:21.306 --> 00:11:24.309
You sure you want to say that?

00:11:24.684 --> 00:11:27.604
Don't worry about me!

00:11:28.646 --> 00:11:30.523
He can hit eight at once, too?

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:35.737
He's hitting all of them to the right?

00:11:35.737 --> 00:11:38.198
He's determined to break
through his right side.

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:41.534
Echizen is at a disadvantage.

00:11:42.285 --> 00:11:45.747
Echizen is concentrating on breaking
through his opponent's right side.

00:11:46.289 --> 00:11:47.332
In other words,

00:11:47.332 --> 00:11:50.210
his opponent needs only
to focus on his right.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:53.963
However, the balls coming at Echizen

00:11:53.963 --> 00:11:56.508
are scattered all over the place.

00:11:56.508 --> 00:11:59.803
Naturally, Echizen will
expend more energy.

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:04.891
You won't get anything
past my right or left.

00:12:04.891 --> 00:12:06.351
We'll see about that.

00:12:09.229 --> 00:12:10.647
N-Nine balls!

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:15.485
Fifteen all.

00:12:16.778 --> 00:12:21.199
Hitting eight balls isn't
anything to brag about here.

00:12:21.199 --> 00:12:23.410
There's always someone better than you.

00:12:38.341 --> 00:12:40.135
Thirty-fifteen.

00:12:40.427 --> 00:12:42.220
E-Echizen...

00:12:43.221 --> 00:12:44.472
Don't lose your cool!

00:12:46.516 --> 00:12:49.978
We fell to the darkest depths.

00:12:51.396 --> 00:12:56.317
We were marked as losers,
and left lying in the dirt.

00:12:57.944 --> 00:13:03.241
Overcome by defeat, we nearly
lost sight of our goal.

00:13:03.658 --> 00:13:08.663
But we rose up from that hell.

00:13:13.084 --> 00:13:14.461
Forty-fifteen.

00:13:16.379 --> 00:13:20.925
You lose the match if you
lose one game, correct?

00:13:22.469 --> 00:13:25.847
He was the one who
led us all the way.

00:13:26.431 --> 00:13:28.099
That's why we

00:13:28.099 --> 00:13:32.812
entrusted that man's racket
with everything we have.

00:13:33.313 --> 00:13:34.272
Am I wrong?

00:13:37.275 --> 00:13:38.693
You're right.

00:13:38.693 --> 00:13:40.904
Who the hell do you think he is?

00:13:40.904 --> 00:13:42.113
He's Koshimae!

00:13:47.118 --> 00:13:50.330
You're finished!

00:14:05.387 --> 00:14:06.763
Do it!

00:14:11.267 --> 00:14:13.061
All right!

00:14:13.061 --> 00:14:14.270
Yeah!

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:14.979
He did it!

00:14:20.318 --> 00:14:23.071
Hitting nine balls is
nothing to brag about.

00:14:26.282 --> 00:14:28.118
T-Ten balls?

00:14:41.673 --> 00:14:44.134
F-Forty-thirty.

00:14:44.134 --> 00:14:46.094
No, that's game.

00:14:47.595 --> 00:14:50.598
He broke through my right side,
just like he said he would.

00:14:51.725 --> 00:14:53.268
I lost.

00:14:54.769 --> 00:14:55.687
Thanks.

00:14:56.062 --> 00:14:57.272
Migihashi.

00:14:57.939 --> 00:15:00.525
We have an announcement
for all players.

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:04.112
As per the coaches' suggestion,

00:15:04.112 --> 00:15:07.032
the 27 losing middle schoolers

00:15:07.032 --> 00:15:09.451
are assigned to Court 2.

00:15:09.451 --> 00:15:12.370
All right!

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:15.290
We made it back from the edge of hell!

00:15:15.999 --> 00:15:17.959
Welcome back, Kin-<i>chan</i>.

00:15:17.959 --> 00:15:19.836
Oishi!

00:15:19.836 --> 00:15:21.880
C-Calm down, Eiji.

00:15:27.969 --> 00:15:31.890
Their growth has been
monstrous as always.

00:16:00.251 --> 00:16:03.213
Captain Tezuka left for Germany?

00:16:03.505 --> 00:16:04.381
Yeah.

00:16:04.631 --> 00:16:05.924
I see.

00:16:05.924 --> 00:16:07.801
He's taken the first
step towards his dream.

00:16:08.385 --> 00:16:10.804
Damn it! What is this crap?

00:16:11.763 --> 00:16:13.056
Kaidoh.

00:16:13.056 --> 00:16:17.185
I thought we were gonna
finish this camp together.

00:16:17.185 --> 00:16:19.479
Every last one of us, until the end.

00:16:19.813 --> 00:16:23.692
I'm sure Tezuka regrets that, too.

00:16:23.692 --> 00:16:24.567
But...

00:16:25.068 --> 00:16:26.152
But?

00:16:26.945 --> 00:16:28.822
Even if we're far apart,

00:16:28.822 --> 00:16:33.368
we'll always be united by tennis.

00:16:33.368 --> 00:16:34.411
Yeah.

00:16:34.828 --> 00:16:36.538
As long as we keep playing tennis,

00:16:36.538 --> 00:16:38.206
I'm sure we'll see him again.

00:16:38.206 --> 00:16:40.041
Even if we have to part ways, right?

00:16:40.041 --> 00:16:42.252
We all proved that.

00:16:42.252 --> 00:16:45.672
We get to play tennis together again.

00:16:47.966 --> 00:16:53.471
Let's carry on Tezuka's spirit
and finish this camp.

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:56.016
All together.

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:00.478
Yes.

00:17:25.795 --> 00:17:27.881
I just don't like this.

00:17:27.881 --> 00:17:29.299
You don't like it?

00:17:29.716 --> 00:17:34.929
How did you losers end up
higher ranked than me?

00:17:34.929 --> 00:17:37.474
Sometimes you win, sometimes you lose.

00:17:37.474 --> 00:17:40.143
We beat them first,
so Court 2 belongs to us.

00:17:40.143 --> 00:17:43.480
Let's play to see who
the real winners are.

00:17:44.397 --> 00:17:48.401
None of you move well
enough for Court 2.

00:17:54.741 --> 00:17:56.076
Interesting.

00:17:56.076 --> 00:17:57.619
Let's settle this, then.

00:17:59.079 --> 00:18:02.540
Kai-<i>kun</i>, you know what that means.

00:18:07.962 --> 00:18:10.465
That's quite the look.

00:18:11.966 --> 00:18:14.678
We look forward to playing you.

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:23.853
Hey.

00:18:24.521 --> 00:18:26.314
I'm here for my revenge.

00:18:32.445 --> 00:18:34.864
Hit that serve again.

00:18:37.033 --> 00:18:41.413
I will be the one to decide
if you are worthy.

00:18:49.004 --> 00:18:50.714
Thanks, Senpai.

00:19:16.948 --> 00:19:18.575
I'll stop it even if it kills me!

00:19:18.575 --> 00:19:20.285
Burning!

00:19:26.291 --> 00:19:27.876
Nice hit!

00:19:32.464 --> 00:19:35.842
You've improved a little, Ryoma Echizen.

00:19:38.678 --> 00:19:42.557
I also returned, one year ago,
wearing that black jersey.

00:19:45.393 --> 00:19:47.771
Is the old man doing well?

00:19:47.771 --> 00:19:48.855
He's doing <i>too </i>well.

00:19:49.606 --> 00:19:51.900
How was the hellish training?

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:54.277
It was fun, actually.

00:19:54.861 --> 00:19:56.029
I'm sure it was.

00:19:56.654 --> 00:20:00.033
I knew you needed to meet Coach Nyudo.

00:20:00.825 --> 00:20:02.202
What do you mean?

00:20:03.036 --> 00:20:05.789
You hate losing more than anyone,

00:20:05.789 --> 00:20:09.292
but you feel excitement,
deep inside, when you do lose.

00:20:09.793 --> 00:20:11.378
Are you different?

00:20:11.378 --> 00:20:12.170
I'm the same.

00:20:13.380 --> 00:20:15.173
I'm disappointed, but excited.

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:16.758
Why?

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:20.679
Because I feel twice the satisfaction
when I win the next time.

00:20:21.221 --> 00:20:22.430
I see.

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:26.059
I guess I'll be feeling
twice the satisfaction today.

00:20:28.478 --> 00:20:29.979
Do you want to go home?

00:20:30.313 --> 00:20:31.898
After I beat you.

00:20:35.694 --> 00:20:37.320
Nice, Oishi.

00:20:38.113 --> 00:20:39.406
Why are you two forming a doubles team

00:20:39.406 --> 00:20:41.157
when you're supposed to be opponents?!

00:20:43.993 --> 00:20:45.620
Good one, Kin-<i>chan</i>.

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:47.664
Ecstasy!

00:20:47.664 --> 00:20:50.083
Court 2 will win!

00:21:04.305 --> 00:21:07.308
Are you ready to face hell again?

00:21:08.059 --> 00:21:11.688
So long as I'm playing tennis,
even hell is fun.

00:21:14.441 --> 00:21:17.944
Not even I know what lies ahead.

00:21:18.486 --> 00:21:21.114
Once we take the first step,
we can't stop,

00:21:21.698 --> 00:21:25.118
even if all our limbs should break!

00:21:25.994 --> 00:21:26.953
Bring it on!

00:21:30.498 --> 00:21:33.168
Fly onwards to your next limit.

00:21:34.294 --> 00:21:35.378
Limit?

00:21:35.837 --> 00:21:37.088
Sorry, but...

00:21:39.215 --> 00:23:17.120
There's still a long way to go.
